            <description><![CDATA[<!doctype html><html><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Lectern 1.5.3</title>
<style>body{font:13px -apple-system,sans-serif;margin:16px;color:#222}h2{margin:0 0 4px}h3{margin:14px 0 4px;color:#7a5af0}
li{margin:3px 0}@media (prefers-color-scheme:dark){body{color:#eee;background:#1e1e1e}}</style></head>
<body><h2>Lectern 1.5.3</h2><p>Flashcards show which slide or page they came from</p><h3>Added</h3><ul><li>New flashcards show which slide or page their information came from (&quot;From Slide 7&quot;, or &quot;Page 3 · Article&quot; for notes from a link or file), checked against your notes. Click it to open that slide beside your notes, or the link or file. Shown when cards are created, in the page&#x27;s flashcards panel, while studying, in decks and in the page&#x27;s Flashcards section. Cards made from highlighted text get their slide too.</li></ul></body></html>]]></description>
